EXT. VAPORETTO STOP, VENICE - EVENING

Gold light on green water. A floating dock. A crowd on a pier. Boats slap at their moorings.

PETRA, 30s, in a red scarf and sensible boots, drags a rolling suitcase onto the dock, while LEOPOLD, 30s, in a rumpled linen suit, sprints from the opposite end holding a bouquet of crushed daisies, and GIULIA, 70s, a nonna in a black shawl, yells from a balcony, and HENRIK, 20s, a tourist with a map, steps between them and drops it, and FATIMA, 30s, a ticket seller in a blue uniform, leans from her booth to shout about the schedule, and ARTHUR, 50s, a silver-haired gentleman, sips an espresso on a bench, watching it all.

PETRA
Leopold?

LEOPOLD
Petra!

GIULIA
(from the balcony)
Leopoldo! Don't let her go!

FATIMA
The last boat leaves in two minutes!

HENRIK
Excuse me, where is the Rialto?

ARTHUR
(to Henrik)
Wherever they are, I'd follow them.

Petra stops. Leopold stops, six feet away. The daisies drop petals on the planks.

LEOPOLD
I was a fool.

PETRA
You were.

LEOPOLD
Stay.

PETRA
The boat.

FATIMA
Ninety seconds!

Petra looks at the boat. At the suitcase. At the daisies.

PETRA
Is that for me?

LEOPOLD
It was a bouquet.

She takes the daisies. Lets go of the suitcase. It rolls into the water. Nobody notices. The boat pulls away.
